Q: Laravel Livewire query with relationship A: <p>I think this error is caused by importing or type-hinting the <strong>wrong <code>Builder</code> class.<br />
This is a namespace issue, not a Livewire or relationship problem.</strong><br />
Import the correct Builder<br />
<code>use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Builder;</code></p>
<p>Make sure you <strong>do not</strong> have this line:</p>
<pre class="lang-php-template prettyprint-override"><code>use App\Livewire\Builder;
</code></pre>
<p>Your query will then work as expected.</p>
<p>I recommend this structure:</p>
<pre class="lang-php-template prettyprint-override"><code>$jobs = Job::with(['getCustomer', 'getOperative', 'getPCode', 'getUrgency'])
    -&gt;where(function ($query) use ($search2) {
        $query-&gt;where('id', 'like', &quot;%{$search2}%&quot;)
              -&gt;orWhere('address', 'like', &quot;%{$search2}%&quot;)
              -&gt;orWhere('cust_ref', 'like', &quot;%{$search2}%&quot;)
              -&gt;orWhereHas('getCustomer', function ($q) use ($search2) {
                  $q-&gt;where('name', 'like', &quot;%{$search2}%&quot;);
              });
    })
    -&gt;orderByDesc('id')
    -&gt;paginate(25);
</code></pre>
